cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: >-
  If you refer to this repository, or reuse its code, prose, or figures, please
  cite it using the metadata below.
title: "Stochastic Systems in Julia"
abstract: >-
  A Julia repository of ten reproducible numerical case studies in probability,
  stochastic processes, and computational statistical physics. Each case study
  states a question, develops the mathematics it rests on, implements the
  numerical method from first principles, and validates the result against an
  analytical or independently computed reference with quantified uncertainty.
  The repository is under active construction and no release has been made.
authors:
  - family-names: "Pérez Flores"
    given-names: "Edgar Axel"
repository-code: "https://github.com/EdgarIFI/numerical-stochastic-systems-julia"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Julia
  - stochastic processes
  - Monte Carlo methods
  - stochastic differential equations
  - molecular dynamics
  - computational statistical physics
  - reproducible research
